    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a challenging slate today, but the optimizer is leaning heavily into favorable hitting conditions for our middle infield core. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Gunnar Henderson** (76.04) stand as our most potent options; **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a substantial +16% park factor and a strong platoon advantage against Kyle Bradish, while **Gunnar Henderson** remains a mandatory start despite facing the high-caliber Gerrit Cole, buoyed by the same venue-driven power ceiling. **Heliot Ramos** (66.19) is also a primary target, as his ability to leverage the park environment keeps him in elite territory despite a modest suppression from his opponent\u2019s efficiency at holding runners.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was excluding **Nasim Nunez** (38.21) from the starting nine. While **Nasim Nunez** offers the elite sprint speed we covet for our stolen base targets, his projection was severely dampened by a projected #9 lineup spot and an unfavorable matchup against Jacob deGrom. The optimizer opted for the higher floor provided by **Sam Antonacci** (63.14), who projects for a much higher frequency of plate appearances at the top of the lineup. We are also monitoring the availability of **Drake Baldwin**, whose score of 65.45 relies on an assumed #2 spot in the order; should **Drake Baldwin** drop lower in the lineup, his value may shift toward our marginal tier.\n\nManagers should proceed with caution regarding the high-end opposition on the mound today. **Coby Mayo** (46.68) and **Dominic Smith** (47.41) are teetering near the bench threshold, as both face tough sequencing or platoon disadvantages that leave little margin for error. We are also continuing to navigate the absences of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (IL) and the scheduled off-days for **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages**. With **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Josh Jung**, and **Curtis Mead** not appearing in today's active rotation, we are relying on our depth players like **Liam Hicks** to maximize our daily efficiency cap without overextending our roster limits.",
